{% set local_problem %}
<p>Cullman's commitment to home maintenance means damaged fascia stands out — both visually and functionally. Peeling paint, water stains, and visible rot detract from otherwise well-maintained properties. More importantly, compromised fascia can't properly support gutters and allows water into roof structures.</p>

<p>Older homes near downtown face particular challenges. Original fascia boards may be approaching or exceeding their natural lifespan. Years of Alabama humidity and occasional gutter problems have taken their toll. These homes deserve repair work that respects their character while restoring full function.</p>

<p>Even newer homes can develop fascia problems if gutters have been overflowing or leaking. Water damage accumulates over time, and rot can spread behind paint that looks fine on the surface.</p>

<p>We inspect fascia carefully on every job. If repair is needed, we address it properly before gutter work — ensuring your new gutters have solid support and your home's appearance is restored.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We begin with thorough inspection — checking not just visible surfaces but probing for hidden damage behind paint and at seams. You'll know exactly what condition your fascia is in.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out rotted wood, and install new fascia boards. We use quality materials appropriate to your home — standard primed lumber for most applications, or matching profiles for historic homes where appearance matters.</p>

<p>New gutters are then installed on solid, properly prepared fascia. The result is a complete system: sound structure supporting quality gutters, designed to prevent the water problems that caused damage in the first place.</p>
{% endset %}

